       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. It carries a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis, and it won't give better glucose control. Glycemic benefit plateaus at about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum).\n- **Another dose within the labeled range** that you choose.\n\nIf you think this dose is intended, for example for a protocol or research use, the order should go through pharmacy review and your institution's high-dose override process. I can't safely enter it directly. Tell me if you'd like to go with one of the options above."
